## Compatibility findings

- Exposed Java `ProcessQueue.REBALANCE_LOCK_MAX_LIVE_TIME` and
  `REBALANCE_LOCK_INTERVAL` through paired Rust accessors. Both values are
  cached together on first queue access and reused by orderly scheduling and
  expiration checks. The property parser accepts Java Unicode decimal digits.
- Mapped private Java `MQClientAPIImpl.sendSmartMsg` to a process-wide Rust
  selector. Producer sends now honor the default-true Java Boolean property;
  normal, reply, and batch request codes follow Java branch order, including
  `MSG_TYPE=reply`.
- Pinned Java invocation fixtures exercise ordinary, reply, and batch request
  selection with the switch both enabled and disabled. Isolated Rust processes
  cover unset, false, uppercase true, whitespace, malformed values, and
  first-access setting capture.
- `ResponseFuture` source reverse audit confirms both declared constructors
  and all 20 public methods are documented; no unmapped capability was found
  in that slice.

